--- body ---
## Context

The REL sweep will run on padme with `scripts/harvest/catalog_openalex.py --resume`.
In `scripts/openalex_pool.py`, `_download_tiers()` currently increments
`queries_completed` and writes today's date to `_query_dates.json` immediately
after `fetch_query()`, even when that query stopped because its API budget was
exhausted. On the next run, `from_created_date` then skips records that were
on unread pages. A 429 response may also leave the current boolean completion
signal ambiguous; `--limit` deliberately stops pagination early.

This ticket covers completion and resume safety. Ticket 0298 separately covers
the periodic `from_updated_date` pass and discovery-recall gate.

## Actions

1. Make `fetch_query()` report whether pagination reached its natural end,
   versus budget exhaustion, rate limiting, an explicit limit, or another
   interruption. Preserve already fetched pool records and their IDs.
2. Advance the per-query date and completed counter only for a fully completed
   query. Leave the previous date unchanged for every partial query, so a
   retry replays its original window and deduplicates records already stored.
3. Ensure an interrupted query stops the sweep without marking remaining
   queries complete; keep sidecar writes safe across interruption/restart.
4. Before the REL sweep, exercise an interrupted and resumed query against a
   deterministic fake paginated API. The test must check the persisted
   sidecar, resulting pool IDs and completed/skipped counts, not only logs.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Budget exhaustion after at least one page and a 429 response leave the
      old query date intact; the next run retrieves every later page once.
- [x] A `--limit` run does not claim a complete query or advance its date.
- [x] A fully paginated query advances its date once; unaffected queries retain
      their own checkpoints.
- [x] Changed-behaviour tests and the required corpus WP gate pass on padme,
      with the corpus available; the PR records the gate and resulting commit.

## Verification

- `7e358d90` `scripts/openalex_pool.py:212,242-258,345-354` separates
  interruption from completed pagination and dates only completed queries;
  `scripts/openalex_pool.py:95-107` replaces the sidecar atomically.
- `7e358d90` `scripts/harvest/catalog_openalex.py:347-349` stops writing the
  legacy global checkpoint, which cannot represent a partial sweep.
- `tests/test_openalex_resume_completion.py::test_interrupted_query_replays_original_window`
  covers both zero budget and HTTP 429, pool IDs, persisted dates, replay and
  the later-query stop; `::test_record_limit_does_not_advance_date` covers
  `--limit`. Both pass locally after the final test edit.
- Padme, clean branch worktree with `make data`: `make check-fast` 2466 passed,
  9 skipped; `make lint` 346 passed, 11 skipped. The unmodified
  `make check-corpus-wp` target failed because it combines two pytest roots
  with conflicting `conftest` imports and because the gitignored reranker
  cache was absent from the new worktree. After copying the existing 2.1 MB
  cache from padme's primary checkout and running the same WP selection by
  root, `tests/ -m wp_corpus` passed (1368 passed, 34 skipped) and the
  package's `-m wp_corpus` passed (25 passed). These gate issues are outside
  this ticket's code diff.
